---
description: Read CivCraft YAML config inline via get*OrDefault; do not add thin CivSettings getter wrappers.
alwaysApply: true
---

# CivSettings config access

Do **not** add static getters on `CivSettings` that only forward to `getStringOrDefault`, `getDoubleOrDefault`, or `getIntegerOrDefault` on a `FileConfiguration`. Call those helpers **at the use site** with the right config object and YAML path.

## Do this

```java
// ✅ GOOD — inline at call site
double repositionDistance = CivSettings.getDoubleOrDefault(
        CivSettings.questSettingsConfig, "guide.reposition_distance", 20.0);

persistence.lastGuideSeasonId = CivSettings.getStringOrDefault(
        CivSettings.questSettingsConfig, "season.id", "");

// Supplier / constructor arg — same pattern
() -> CivSettings.getStringOrDefault(CivSettings.questSettingsConfig, "season.id", "")
```

Use the static `FileConfiguration` field that owns the YAML (`questSettingsConfig`, `townSettingsConfig`, `civConfig`, etc.) and keep defaults in the **third argument** of `get*OrDefault`, matching `data/*.yml`.

## Do not do this

```java
// ❌ BAD — thin wrapper on CivSettings
public static double getGuideRepositionDistance() {
    return getDoubleOrDefault(questSettingsConfig, "guide.reposition_distance", 20.0);
}

// ❌ BAD — call site still goes through wrapper
CivSettings.getGuideRepositionDistance();
```

## When a CivSettings method is OK

- Loads or parses config (e.g. `loadCivConfig`, storage `init` wiring)
- Combines multiple keys, validates, or applies non-trivial defaults
- Same path read in **many** places with **non-trivial** derived logic — prefer a `private` helper on the class that owns the workflow, not a new public `CivSettings` getter unless the user asks

## Agent behavior

When adding or changing tunables in `data/*.yml`, update the YAML and use `get*OrDefault` inline where the value is consumed. Remove existing thin getters if you touch their call sites.
